# INV-14 — invented. Twenty overs a side: a long match, scored to the last ball.
# Edge cases: five bowlers, four overs each, in rotation (never two overs
# running); a maiden-heavy spell (BW1: 4-3-13-1, with a bye in one maiden, a
# leg bye in another and a wicket in the third; his one expensive over has a
# no-ball and the free hit hit for six); a hat-trick (BW3, in the 3rd over:
# bowled, caught, lbw on three balls running, the batters falling at 10 for
# 1, 2 and 3: "2.3", "2.4", "2.5"); a fifty (B5: 59 off 42); a wicket on the
# last ball of an over (falls at 6.6); a chase of 148 that reaches it on the
# very last ball, nine down: won by one wicket.
# The milestones the fold gives are stated on the card (fifty, hat-trick).
